node_modules/
out/
dist/
release/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Working copies of this same repository.
#
# A git worktree under here holds a COMPLETE second copy of the tree, so a bare
# `prettier --check .` walks the project twice and reports every file in the
# other copy as unformatted — including files from a milestone that predates the
# formatter. It passed inside a worktree and failed in the checkout beside it,
# which is the wrong way round for a gate to behave (issues.md I-20).
.claude/

# npm writes it; npm's shape is the right shape.
package-lock.json

# Deliberately broken, so the audits can be proved to bite. Formatting them
# would be tidying a thing whose whole job is to be wrong.
tests/fixtures/

# ── PROSE IS THE MAKER'S ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# XTRITIUM is the constitution and the F-documents are its record. Both are
# hand-set: wrapped where the sentences want to break, with tables aligned by
# eye and paragraphs shaped to be read. Prettier would reflow all of it to a
# printWidth and destroy an authorship the project has kept for twelve
# milestones.
#
# The formatter serves the code. The prose does not need serving.
*.md
